 ## 2026-07-20
 
+### 2317 — M1 runtime contract separates structural work from production M0 binding (TASK-260715-30zng6)
+- DECISION: The packet-tunnel extension owns one actor-serialized runtime generation, with immutable app-message snapshots and no live forwarding dependency on the containing app. Startup is configuration -> verified/authenticated SSH -> TCP/DNS readiness -> pure packet preflight -> settings apply -> existing PacketBridge.start/read activation -> TCP + safe-DNS publication; every failure rolls back through one idempotent, non-cancellable stopping path.
+- OWNERSHIP: M1PacketPlaneSession is the sole owner of the HEV private SOCKS boundary and dispatches authenticated CONNECT to TCP plus only approved virtual-DNS UDP/TCP to DNS; other UDP is rejected until M2. The coordinator proceeds against fakes independently of production factories, and both branches converge at TASK-260715-30ugfm.
+- M0 GATE: TASK-260715-nphtib, TASK-260715-2jatnd, and TASK-260715-1gjxer currently have no reviewer-accepted outcome resources. New atomic TASK-260720-1qhxqa binds their future exact resources/digests and alone may set productionCompositionPermitted=true; TASK-260715-3ejhyy remains blocked behind it without delaying candidate-neutral models/coordinator work.
+- SAFETY: Settings clear is called only after a committed or uncertain apply. A required failed/uncertain clear publishes capabilities false but truthfully retains routesInstalled=true with routeState=clearFailed; a clear that was unnecessary or confirmed publishes routesInstalled=false. Legacy version protocol v1 remains byte-exact while new M1 commands/snapshots use explicit schemas.
+- REVIEW: Independent agent review requested and verified corrections across ownership, source-interface feasibility, versions, dependencies, transitions, and route cleanup, then accepted all five AC. PlantUML is unavailable and local Graphviz is broken by missing libltdl; authoritative sources and the toolchain anomaly are attached rather than claiming rendered evidence.
+
 ### 2158 — Shared relay hostile corpus is semantically identical in Swift and Go (TASK-260715-297gq6)
 - IMPLEMENTATION: Both protocol bindings consume the checked `lcg64-v1` regression corpus. Four fixed 64-bit seeds drive 2,096 deterministic cases across both envelope directions, legal and mutated frames, hostile declared lengths, arbitrary chunking/coalescing, inner HEV parsing, EOF, cancellation, and reset. Each language derives the same four stable semantic digests, so code/phase/scope/disposition or ordering drift fails the common gate without comparing implementation-specific error text.
 - REVIEW REWORK: Decoder metrics now count internal byte/prefix/header/frame processing iterations and current/peak body-allocation bytes. Shared prefix-only cases declare exactly 4,096 bytes and 4,097 bytes, proving the accepted ceiling allocates at most 4,096 bytes and the next value allocates zero. The deterministic work ceiling is `inputBytes + 3 × bodyAllocations + 1`.

Contract, diagrams, task decomposition, dependency routing, validation evidence, logbook entry, and autonomous reviewer acceptance are all in place. The only remaining action is the required role handoff status change.
